.TH "CSSSTYLEVALUE.TOSTRING" "3JS" "August 4, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSStyleValue.toString \- CSSStyleValue: toString() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]toString()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]CSSStyleValue\f[R] interface is a stringifier that returns the
value formatted as a string of standard CSS text.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toString()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A string.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The exact serialization of the object to a string depends on how the
\f[CR]CSSStyleValue\f[R] object was obtained:
.IP \(bu 2
If the object was created by parsing a CSS string, such as with
\f[CR]CSSStyleValue.parse()\f[R], the method returns the original string
that was parsed.
.IP \(bu 2
If the object was constructed directly, such as with a \f[CR]CSS\f[R]
factory function or a subclass constructor, the returned string is
generated according to serialization rules specific to that subclass.
.IP \(bu 2
If the object was read from the CSSOM, such as with
\f[CR]Element.computedStyleMap()\f[R] or
\f[CR]HTMLElement.attributeStyleMap\f[R], the returned string follows
the CSSOM serialization rules.
.PP
For more information about serialization rules see When and how values
are serialized in \f[I]CSS value serialization\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// Parsed from a string: returns the original string\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] length1 = CSSStyleValue.parse(\(dq42.0px\(dq);
length1.toString(); \f[I]// \(dq42.0px\(dq\f[R]

\f[I]// Constructed directly with a CSS factory function: subclass\-specific serialization\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] length2 = CSS.px(42.0);
length2.toString(); \f[I]// \(dq42px\(dq\f[R]

\f[I]// Read from the CSSOM: follows CSSOM serialization rules\f[R]
\f[B]const\f[R] element = document.createElement(\(dqdiv\(dq);
element.style.width = \(dq42.0px\(dq;
\f[B]const\f[R] length3 = element.attributeStyleMap.get(\(dqwidth\(dq);
length3.toString(); \f[I]// \(dq42px\(dq\f[R]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Using the CSS Typed OM
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSStyleValue.parse()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]CSSStyleValue.parseAll()\f[R]
